  - `detail::FixedTagChecker`

In `hwy/ops/shared-inl.h`, the alias is documented as:

> “Alias for a tag describing a vector with *exactly* `kNumLanes` active lanes, even on targets with scalable vectors. Requires `kNumLanes` to be a power of two not exceeding `HWY_LANES(T)`.”

The actual alias is:

```cpp
template <typename T, size_t kNumLanes>
using FixedTag = typename detail::FixedTagChecker<T, kNumLanes>::type;
```

and `FixedTagChecker` resolves it to:

```cpp
template <typename T, size_t kNumLanes>
struct FixedTagChecker {
  static_assert(kNumLanes != 0, "Does not make sense to have zero lanes");
  static_assert(kNumLanes <= HWY_LANES(T), "Too many lanes");
  using type = Simd<T, kNumLanes, 0>;
};
```

The same file explicitly contrasts it with `CappedTag`:

```cpp
// NOTE: if the application does not need to support HWY_SCALAR (+), use this
// instead of CappedTag to emphasize that there will be exactly kNumLanes lanes.
```

So the answer is: **use `FixedTag<T, kNumLanes>` instead of `CappedTag` when you require exactly `kNumLanes` active lanes.**

